As you may or may not know the normally aspirated engine rebuild that I went through
turned out a complete disaster. Not only did the engine consume excessive amounts
of oil it didn't produce anything like the power I was promised. To finish things
off the cam belt snapped on the rebuilt engine in November 2000. I am in the
middle of issuing legal proceedings against the garage that carried out the work.
<P>
I was initially waiting for the case to be heard in court and an outcome reached
before deciding what to do next. This is taking longer than I thought and feel
I have suffered enough with the car. I'm therefore going the engine rebuilt
as soon as possible on the basis that I need a car no matter what the outcome of
the court case.
<P>
I'm going for a turbo charged engine this time, infact a complete engine
transplant rather than a &quot;bolt on&quot; jobbie. There are three engines that
are possible candidates: A Lancia Thema 2.0 16V Turbo, a Fiat Coupe 2.0 16V Turbo and
a Lancia Integrale 2.0 16V Turbo. The advantage of going for one of these engines is that
they have been designed, tested and built around a Turbo. That means they are a known
quantity rather than a specialised engine with unknown characteristics.
<P>
I know that the price is not going to be cheap and you may be thinking why don't
you just buy another car. Well to be honest I think that the Tipo is hard to
beat and is almost everything I want in a car (of course an Evo 5,6 or 7 would
be nice but I don't have that sort of money). I know the complete history of
my car and know it's had the best care. To me the Tipo's main attributes are:
<UL>
<LI>It's understated.
<LI>It's so rare that hardly anyone knows what it is.
<LI>It's Italian and has a certain charm to it.
<LI>The interior space is huge compared to modern cars with their curvy lines.
<LI>It handles reasonably well.
<LI>It's great fun to drive without having to go fast.
<LI>The feedback from the steering is superb.
</UL>

<P>
The following will hopefully be an account of the whole process.
<P>
<FONT SIZE=+1>I
would like to say a huge thank you to Andy Forsdyke, George Roberts,
Aleksandar Medo and Alex Neagu for all their advice and help with this project.</FONT>
<P>

